  <title>Lagrange Multipliers</title>
   <introduction>
    <p>
     Power series, Taylor series and Taylor polynomials are all useful tools, since they can replace a function like <m>\sin(x)</m> with a polynomial function. In physics
     and engineering applications, a Taylor polynomial approximation is often sufficient to produce a useful solution.

    </p>
  </introduction>
  
